ents with rabbit allergy with the addition of rabbit (&#x025cf;), cat (&#x025a0;), and dog (&#x025b2;) epithelia and <italic>D. pteronyssinus</italic> (&#x025c6;) extracts.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-22-820-g003"/></fig><fig id="F4" position="float"><label>Fig. 4</label><caption><p>IgE (<bold>A</bold>) and IgG<sub>4</sub> (<bold>B</bold>) immunoblot analysis for rabbit epithelium in sera from three sensitized patients (1-3), nonatopic controls (n), and buffer controls (b).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-22-820-g004"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Clinical characteristics and specific IgE levels to rabbit epithelium in study subjects</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-22-820-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>FHx, family history; BA, bronchial asthma; AR, allergic rhinitis; AC, allergic conjunctivitis; AD, atopic dermatitis.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>